---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const updated = "October 28, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Bitterroot Boudoir collects and uses contact and site information in Stevensville, Montana."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap privacy">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-delay-1">How I handle your information.</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-delay-2">
        I collect only what I need to run the business and serve clients — nothing is sold.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated reveal reveal-delay-3">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap privacy-body">
      <section>
        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>
          When you use the contact form or email me, I may receive your name,
          email address, phone number (if you share it), package interest, hair
          &amp; makeup preference, and the message you write. If we work
          together, I may also keep booking, session, and delivery details needed
          to complete your experience.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why I use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To reply to inquiries and plan sessions</li>
          <li>To manage bookings, artwork, and client communication</li>
          <li>
            To send occasional studio updates or offers by email or phone once a
            mailing list is active — you can opt out anytime
          </li>
          <li>
            To measure advertising and site performance (including Google Ads
            conversion and related tracking when those tools are turned on)
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Formspree and other tools</h2>
        <p>
          Contact form submissions may be processed by
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Formspree</a
          >
          and delivered to my business inbox. Formspree acts as a service
          provider for that handoff. I may also use email or CRM tools to keep
          contact lists organized, and Google Ads / Google analytics-style tools
          to understand whether ads and pages are working. Those providers
          process data under their own privacy terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies and ads</h2>
        <p>
          When Google Ads or similar measurement is active, cookies or similar
          technologies may be used to track visits, ad clicks, and conversions.
          This helps me know what’s effective — not to build a dossier on you.
          You can limit ad personalization through your browser settings and
          Google’s ad settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Inquiry and client records are kept as long as they’re useful for
          follow-up, active work, or ordinary business records, then removed or
          archived when no longer needed. Mailing-list contacts stay until you
          unsubscribe or ask to be removed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          Email
          <a href="mailto:hello@bitterrootboudoir.com">hello@bitterrootboudoir.com</a>
          to ask what I have on file, correct something, or request deletion /
          removal from updates. For marketing messages, use the unsubscribe link
          when available, or just reply and ask to be taken off the list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          I don’t sell your information. I only share what’s needed with trusted
          processors (like Formspree, email hosts, or ad platforms) to run the
          site and studio, or when the law requires it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="privacy-note">
        This page is a practical studio notice, not formal legal advice. If my
        tools or practices change in a meaningful way, I’ll update it here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy .lede {
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .privacy-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .privacy-body section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .privacy-body h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
  }

  .privacy-body p,
  .privacy-body li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .privacy-body p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .privacy-body ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .privacy-body a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.45);
  }

  .privacy-note {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
